    "faqLabel": "Frequently asked questions",
    "faqTitle": "Good to know",
    "faqSeeAll": "See all questions →",
    "faq": {
      "1": { "q": "How do I book a boat on SailingLoc?", "a": "Search by port, dates and number of guests. Choose a listing, click « Book » and follow the steps through to secure payment." },
      "2": { "q": "Can I cancel my booking?", "a": "Yes, from « My bookings ». Refunds depend on the owner's cancellation policy and how far in advance you cancel." },
      "3": { "q": "Are boats insured?", "a": "Each owner must provide valid navigation insurance. SailingLoc checks these documents before publishing the listing." },
      "4": { "q": "Can I rent a boat with a skipper?", "a": "Yes, if the owner offers it. Use the « with skipper » filter in search to find suitable listings." },
      "5": { "q": "What are the service fees?", "a": "SailingLoc charges around 10% service fees to the renter. The exact amount is always shown before confirmation." },
      "6": { "q": "How does the deposit work?", "a": "The owner may set a deposit amount in the listing. It is shown for information only; the actual hold or deposit is arranged directly between renter and owner before departure." },
      "7": { "q": "How do I list my boat for rent?", "a": "Create an owner account, click « Add a boat », fill in the details and add photos. The listing goes live after verification." },
      "8": { "q": "When does the owner receive payment?", "a": "The renter pays online via Stripe when booking. Owner payouts are tracked in the Revenues dashboard. Automatic payouts via Stripe Connect are planned for phase 2." }
    },
